  "details": "In the settings, there is an option to \"skip go button on load\"\n\nBy default, I think this is off. You would see a button that says go where you would load in and a button to go home.\n\nI think it might be nice that if you have this setting disabled (so you still see the \"go\" button) you could do small things before you actually load into the world. Things like maybe changing your avatar, changing your shield level, changing your status color, maybe change volume controls or enable earmuffs before entering... \n\nThere has been a few times where I joined someone and was in an avatar I didn't want to be in. It could give a reason to have the \"disable go\" button turned off. I think it could add a bit more ease of use to switching between worlds.",
